      "originalTitle": "fix(interceptors): tolerate nullish handlers in syncHandlerEntries",
      "body": ":surfer:\n\nFixes #11114\n\n## Problem\n\n`syncHandlerEntries()` reads `handlers.length` before checking that `handlers` exists, so assigning a falsy value to the public `handlers` array makes every subsequent request throw:\n\n```js\naxios.interceptors.request.use(config => config);\naxios.interceptors.request.handlers = null;\nawait axios.get('https://example.com');\n// TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'length')\n```\n\n`clear()` has always guarded with `if (this.handlers)`, and `utils.forEach` returns early on nullish input, so a falsy `handlers` array was a tolerated state on v1.19.0. This is a regression from #11087 (merged, unreleased).\n\n## Fix\n\nThree reads were unguarded, not one:\n\n- `syncHandlerEntries` — the `else if (handlers.length !== ...)` branch **and** the trailing `internals.handlersLength = handlers.length`. Both now use a `countHandlers()` helper that treats nullish as an empty stack.\n- `trimHandlers` — returns early instead of dereferencing.\n- the `forEach` `finally` block — `internals.handlersLength = this.handlers.length` had the same problem and now goes through the same helper.\n\nFixing only `syncHandlerEntries` leaves the `finally` block throwing on the way out of the first `forEach`, so both paths are covered.\n\n## Tests\n\n8 cases, parametrized over `null` and `undefined`:\n\n- `forEach` is a no-op rather than throwing\n- a **repeated** `forEach` stays safe — this takes the `handlers === handlersRef` branch, which is where the stack trace in the report actually lands, and it isn't reached by a single call\n- `eject` does not throw\n- the manager recovers once `handlers` is restored to an array\n\nAll 8 fail on `v1.x` with the reported `TypeError` and pass with this change.\n\n## Verification\n\n`npx vitest run --project unit`: **1001 passed, 1 failed**. The single failure is `tests/unit/adapters/fetch.test.js > should not use inherited Symbol.iterator for request headers`, which fails identically on a clean checkout — unrelated to this change. `npx eslint lib/core/InterceptorManager.js` is clean.\n\n## Not included\n\nThe report mentions two further items from the same change, deliberately left out to keep this focused on the crash — happy to follow up on either:\n\n- `eject(String(id))` silently no-ops now that lookups go through a `Map` rather than an array index.\n- `tests/unit/core/InterceptorManager.test.js:32` indexes handlers by id, which only holds while nothing below those slots is trimmed.\n\nNo `PRE_RELEASE_CHANGELOG.md` entry: per `AGENTS.md` that file tracks user-visible unreleased changes, and this crash never shipped — v1.19.0 behaves correctly. Happy to add one if you'd prefer it recorded.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nPrevents a TypeError when interceptor handlers are set to null or undefined by treating them as empty and restoring them on `use()`. Previously `syncHandlerEntries` and the `forEach` cleanup read `.length` unguarded and could crash; now both paths are safe and behavior matches prior tolerant releases.\n\n**Details**\n- Adds `countHandlers()` and uses it in `syncHandlerEntries` and the `forEach` `finally` block to guard nullish stacks.\n- Makes `trimHandlers()` return early for nullish handlers.\n- Updates `use()` to initialize a nullish `handlers` array to `[]` so adding a handler recovers the manager.\n- Changes are limited to `lib/core/InterceptorManager.js`.\n\n**Testing and Docs**\n- Adds 8 unit tests covering null/undefined: `forEach` is a no-op, repeated `forEach` is safe, `eject` does not throw, and adding a handler after a nullish stack works.\n- Suggest updating `/docs/` to clarify that while `handlers` is public, consumers should prefer `eject()`/`clear()`; if set to `null`/`undefined`, `axios` treats it as empty and `use()` restores it.\n- Semantic version impact: Patch.\n\n<sup>Written for commit a56dd3c4674754f594ac4f138845003ea88283e9. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/axios/axios/pull/11118?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n",
